shairport-sync-ma-format.patch: let shairport-sync play Music Assistant's fixed buffered AirPlay 2 stream.

Music Assistant's AirPlay 2 sender (airplay-cli 0.5.11 and later) names each buffered packet's format in
its SSRC as Apple senders do: the audio format's bit index in the top byte. Its default format, ALAC
44.1 kHz/16-bit, then arrives as 0x12000000, which shairport-sync 5.6.3 doesn't know (its code for that
format, 0x0000FACE, was made up) and drops as an unknown SSRC, so the stream plays as silence. This is
upstream's own fix, commit deb8384858b72bb7e4a707c973187298ffcdbabf on the development branch
(https://github.com/mikebrady/shairport-sync/issues/2319), which Music Assistant's developers tested with
their sender. TECHO5 issue #664.

Applied last, after shairport-sync-stdout-delay.patch and shairport-sync-ssrc0-fallback.patch, against
shairport-sync 5.6.3. Drop it when shairport-sync 5.6.4 is tagged and build-shairport-sync.sh moves to it.

--- a/player.h
+++ b/player.h
@@ -151,7 +151,7 @@
 // Dolby Atmos seems to be 7P1
 typedef enum {
   SSRC_NONE = 0,
-  ALAC_44100_S16_2 = 0x0000FACE, // this is made up
+  ALAC_44100_S16_2 = 0x12000000,
   ALAC_48000_S24_2 = 0x15000000,
   ALAC_44100_S24_2 = 0x0000FAC4, // made up: buffered ALAC 44.1k/24 from SSRC-0 senders
   AAC_44100_F24_2 = 0x16000000,
